From 196f6a549d059691a8f273c84fbb6af54d34cd60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 23:18:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00889/11362] [outer-loop] On-policy gen fix: MiniCPM5 is a
 reasoning model -> use enable_thinking=False

Diagnosed the 100% sampling-truncation wall: MiniCPM5-1B is a REASONING model that
generates 900+ token <think> chains and OVER-THINKS GSM8K (gets confused at temp,
'cannot compute... unclear', never terminates). The p01 traces were made in NO-THINK mode
(empty <think></think> marker) -- so the fix is enable_thinking=False in apply_chat_template
(both generation + eval) -> concise direct answers that terminate. Also +repetition_penalty
1.3, temp 0.6, gen cap 1024. Smoke: gen_trunc 1.0->0.667 @512, base eval terminates (trunc
0.0). Launching full on-policy run; instrumentation (truncation guard + gold-control gate)
will report validity honestly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
